# Monaco / CODE IDE — chat handoff

## Where to work

- **Dogfood (8090):** `C:\Projects\AdventureLand\adventureland_mongodb` on `server/local-dev`. Edit here so hard-refresh picks up `js/code/**` + CSS. Rebuild host only when `tools/monaco-vscode-build/src/**` changes: `cd tools/monaco-vscode-build && npm run build`.
- **Feature branch worktree:** `C:\Projects\AdventureLand\adventureland_mongodb-monaco-editor` → `feature/monaco-editor`.
- **Promote stack:** `feature/monaco-editor` → `integration/local-dev-server-misc` → `integration/local-dev-server` → `server/local-dev` (matching worktrees `*-local-dev-misc`, `*-local-dev-server`).

## Rules (must follow)

1. Prefer stock **monaco-vscode-api** patterns (`StandaloneServices`, overrides, `render*Part`, commands, views). See `.cursor/rules/monaco-proper-wiring.mdc`.
2. **Never** patch `node_modules/@codingame/*` or upstream monaco. Host only: `tools/monaco-vscode-build/src/*`, `js/code/**`.
3. Unavoidable workarounds in **our** code get `HACK(monaco):` / Why / Purpose / Remove when.
4. Types: `types/shared` (no top-level `declare`), `types/monaco`, `types/client`, `types/server`. Monaco pack = shared+monaco via `types/monaco/manifest.js` + `agentic/rebuild_monaco_types_bundle.js`. No typed-adventureland regen in that path.
5. After JS edits under `node/`: `npx prettier --check` / `--write` from `node/`. Keep files under ~1k lines when practical.

## Architecture snapshot

- Boot: `js/monaco/vscode-api/monaco-vscode.min.js` → `window.ALVscodeApi` + `window.monaco` (`entry.js`).
- Keys: workbench `updateUserKeybindings` + `alGameCommands` when IDE focused; chrome capture only for browser-stolen chords or Phaser-focused IDE chords.
- Quick Open: stock files; AL provider prefix `al `.
- Hover: themed fence + Types row with `command:` links (no MutationObserver).
- Explorer/Problems title actions via `registerExtension` menus.
- Outline / Explorer / Search: stock SIDEBAR; Problems: stock PANEL_PART; status bar + AL extras.
- Current-char: `IDecorationsService`. Types: raw on `types/`, augment under `types-augment/`.

